Z||000000||ChadMan||08-02-99||08:24 AM||||The Nationals are less than two weeks away and I'm excited.  In the spirit of the moment I thought I'd ask you all a question:  What's the coolest Fiero you've ever seen?  Where was it?  What made it so special?<p>For me, it would have to be an '86 GT that won Best of Show at the 1996 Nationals in Indianapolis.  It was a convertible with tan leather interior, pearlescent paint and a supercharged 3800 Buick motor.  It was absolutely gorgeous and the owner was selling it for $25,000.  I don't know what he got for it, but it was sweet.
Z||000001||Cooter||08-02-99||06:13 PM||||The coolest Fiero would have to be my fastback 4 cyl se! Just kidding. Probably the 84 Indy pace car edition was one of the best looking from the factory.
